Upon receipt of an appeal, if the Appellate Authority so desires, it may:  
- Call for comments from the Competent Authority;  
- Provide an opportunity for a personal hearing to the appellant agency;  
- Examine the facts of the case, the documents on record, and the submissions of the appellant agency;  
- Pass an appropriate order before the period of debarment expires, which may either:  
  - Uphold the Competent Authority’s decision, with or without any variation or a lesser period of Holiday Listing; or  
  - Annul the order of the Competent Authority.  

(Procurement of Goods Manual, p. 55)

