** Consultancy services may be procured when:  
- (i) the organization lacks the in‑house capability or capacity for the required expertise;  
- (ii) a qualified consultant is needed to deliver a specialized, high‑quality service;  
- (iii) impartial advice is required to avoid conflicts of interest;  
- (iv) the engagement will transfer knowledge, provide training, or build capacity;  
- (v) information is needed to identify or implement new methods and systems;  
- (vi) planning and implementing organizational change is necessary; or  
- (vii) even if internal capacity exists, considerations of economy, speed, and efficiency regarding staff, technology, money, or time justify external consultancy.  

**Rationale:** These criteria are explicitly listed in the manual as the justifications for procuring consultancy services, ensuring such purchases address specific gaps or needs that cannot be met internally. (Procurement of Consultancy and Other Services Manual, p. 13)

